/Some simple expressions, to see if the assembler does them right.
/It is a challenge to get both:
/	SZA CLA^2	/7500, and
/	TAD FOO+1	/*not* "TAD FOO"+1
/right.  On the one hand space (OR) is treated like any other operator,
/and evaluation is strictly left to right.  On the other, the MRI needs
/a fully evaluated target address expression before correct code can be
/generated.
*200
	TAD FOO		/ Needs a literal
	TAD FOO+1	/ Needs a *different* literal!
	TAD (-214+212
	TAD (-214+212
	TAD (-212+207
	4;HLT	/ hmm
start,	/ begin here
	1-2-3
	1^2^3
	1-2^3
	1^2-3
	SZA CLA
	SZA CLA^2
	CIF CDF 10
	JMP 10
	JMP I .
*.-1 177+1	/ This one is fun
	NOP
	PAGE
FOO,
	FIELD
$
